ocean_hackathon_data — licence summary
=======================================

Canonical repository: https://github.com/senesh2006/ocean_hackathon_data
Copyright (c) 2026 Senesh Fernando (GitHub: senesh2006)

This repository is a DATA LIBRARY. It mixes original work by the maintainer with
third-party data. Different parts are under different licences:

1. ORIGINAL CODE (all *.py scripts in this repository)
   Licensed under the MIT License (full text below and in LICENSES/MIT.txt).

2. ORIGINAL COMPILATION, DOCUMENTATION AND METADATA
   (README/CHANGELOG/DATA*.md files, catalog.*, data_dictionary.*, data_library.*,
   CITATION.cff, the selection/arrangement of the compiled datasets, QC summaries,
   computed tables such as moon phase and the monsoon calendar, and the
   srilanka-banned-marine compilation)
   Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
   Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

3. THIRD-PARTY DATA KEEPS ITS ORIGINAL LICENCE
   Every data file and every record that comes from (or is derived from) a third-party
   source stays under that source's licence. Nothing in this repository relicenses it.
   The licence of each file is listed in data_library.csv (columns `license`,
   `license_url`, `commercial_use_ok`, `attribution`, `license_note`) and summarised
   in DATA_LIBRARY.md. Where a file combines several sources, the MOST RESTRICTIVE
   licence applies to the file as a whole. In particular:

   * CC BY-NC 4.0 parts are NON-COMMERCIAL ONLY: FishBase-derived tables
     (srilanka-fish-morphology/, fish-data/fishbase/, fish-data/species_list.csv,
     fish-factors/species_flags/), Global Fishing Watch effort (Fishing_sl.csv), and
     OBIS/GBIF records whose `license_norm` is CC-BY-NC-4.0. Any file that contains
     such records (fish-data/obis, gbif, merged, train_ready feature tables, qc audit
     rows) is non-commercial as a whole unless you filter to CC0/CC-BY records.
     Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt
   * CC BY-SA 4.0 parts are SHARE-ALIKE: BOLD Systems barcode data and anything derived
     from it (srilanka-fish-genetics/ BOLD files, species_barcode_coverage.csv,
     qc/sequenced_taxa_not_in_v3_occurrence_list.csv). Adapted material must be shared
     under CC BY-SA 4.0. Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt
   * CC0 1.0 records (some OBIS/GBIF records) are public-domain dedicated.
     Full text: LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt
   * UNEP-WCMC coral reefs (fish-factors/coral_reefs_avoid/, and the coral_reef /
     trawl_candidate columns of fish-factors/seabed_shelf_habitat/) are under the
     UNEP-WCMC General Data License: non-commercial use, citation required
     (doi:10.34892/t2wk-5t34).
   * US Government works (NOAA, NASA, NCEI: SST, winds, SLA, currents, SMAP, WOA23,
     ETOPO, GPCP, DMI/ONI) are public domain in the US; please cite the source.
     CHIRPS (UCSB Climate Hazards Center) is public domain; please cite Funk et al. 2015.
   * IOTC nominal catch: public, with acknowledgement of the IOTC Secretariat required.
   * NCBI GenBank: NCBI places no restrictions on use; some submitters may claim
     patent or copyright on particular sequences.
   * WoRMS name data: CC BY 4.0. ESA OC-CCI chlorophyll: CC BY 4.0.
   * Files whose licence is "unknown" in data_library.csv (currently
     splitwater_ro_log_1h_5s.csv) have no licence grant: all rights reserved until
     the owner confirms.

   Attribution for third-party sources is given per file in data_library.csv and in
   CITATION.cff (references). Regulatory data in srilanka-banned-marine/ is NOT
   legal advice.

THIS DATA IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND.

